{
  "pattern": "listFocus",
  "doc": "Keyboard focus and selection in a list of rows, such as a menu, a channel list or a picker: arrows, Home and End, typeahead, and what happens when the rows change under the focus, and the selection set from outside the list.",
  "params": {
    "wrap": false,
    "selectionFollowsFocus": false,
    "typeaheadMs": "motion.typeahead"
  },
  "state": {
    "rows": "Row[]: in display order, the whole list (not only the rendered window of a virtualised list). Row = {id: string, label: string, disabled: bool}",
    "focused": "string | null: the focused row; never a disabled one",
    "selected": "string | null: the selected row",
    "typeahead": "string: the characters typed so far, folded (rule 16)",
    "token": "int: the token of the latest typeahead timer"
  },
  "events": {
    "setRows": {
      "rows": "Row[]: the new rows, after an add, a removal or a change"
    },
    "focusIn": {},
    "up": {},
    "down": {},
    "home": {},
    "end": {},
    "type": {
      "char": "string: exactly one Unicode scalar value. While the typeahead buffer is not empty, the host sends Space as type, not activate"
    },
    "timerFired": {
      "token": "int"
    },
    "activate": {},
    "press": {
      "id": "string: a pointer press on a row"
    },
    "setSelected": {
      "id": "string | null: the screen's selection, set from outside the list (a route, a value prop)"
    }
  },
  "effects": {
    "select": {
      "id": "string: the row was chosen"
    },
    "startTimer": {
      "token": "int",
      "ms": "int"
    },
    "cancelTimer": {
      "token": "int"
    },
    "deselect": {}
  },
  "rules": [
    "Only enabled rows take focus: every movement skips disabled rows.",
    "With no rows, or only disabled rows, every key does nothing and nothing is focused.",
    "Down moves to the next enabled row and Up to the previous one. With nothing focused, Down focuses the first enabled row and Up the last.",
    "At the ends, Down and Up stay put unless wrap is on; with wrap on (off by default) they go round to the other end.",
    "Home focuses the first enabled row and End the last.",
    "Focus entering the list (focusIn) with no row focused goes to the selected row if it is enabled, otherwise to the first enabled row. It never changes the selection.",
    "Typing a character adds it, folded (rule 16), to the typeahead buffer and restarts the typeahead timer with a new token, cancelling the old one. Focus moves to the first enabled row, from the focused row onwards and going round, whose folded label starts with the buffer.",
    "When the buffer is one character, or one character repeated, typing steps through the rows that start with that character, from the row after the focused one.",
    "When no row matches, focus stays where it is and the buffer still grows.",
    "When the typeahead timer fires with the current token, the buffer empties. Any other token does nothing.",
    "With selectionFollowsFocus off (the default), moving focus never selects. activate (Enter or Space) selects the focused row and emits select{id}, even when it was already selected. activate with nothing focused does nothing.",
    "With selectionFollowsFocus on, every focus move by a key or by typeahead also selects the new row and emits select{id}.",
    "A press on an enabled row focuses and selects it and emits select{id}. A press on a disabled or unknown row does nothing.",
    "When the rows change and the focused row is gone or now disabled, focus moves to the nearest enabled row after it in the old order that is still there, otherwise the nearest one before it, otherwise the first enabled row, otherwise nothing. With selectionFollowsFocus on, the selection moves with it and select{id} is emitted; with it off, the selection stays.",
    "When the selected row is gone from the rows and no move selected another, the selection clears and deselect is emitted.",
    "Typeahead ignores case by folding: each character is mapped on its own with the Unicode default lower-case mapping, which does not depend on the locale (Python str.lower() applied to one character at a time, so the final-sigma rule never applies). Folded text is compared by Unicode scalar values, so an emoji matches only itself.",
    "setSelected sets the selection from outside the list, as a route or a value prop changes it: selected becomes id when id is a row (enabled or disabled), and null when id is null or names no row. It emits nothing, and the focus, the typeahead buffer and its timer are unchanged. It is not a key, so it applies in an empty or all-disabled list too."
  ],
